From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: report no image address; there is no auxiliary vector.

With the mapping fixed, load_main_exe maps Oblivion and start_main_thread
carries on to get_image_address, which faults at address 0:

    PW_WINE64 fault signal=0xb addr=0x0 rip=0x8008ef49a
                                        ntdll+0xbf49a = __getauxval

A title has no auxiliary vector, and this console's getauxval does not answer
that with 0 -- it dereferences and faults. Report no image address instead,
which is what every platform without an auxv does here; the value only reaches
peb->CloudFileFlags.

Only this caller is affected. The auxv is read in three other places and none
is reachable: one is behind __linux__ and this is FreeBSD, and the other two
are on the ARM feature paths.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -1839,7 +1839,18 @@ static void load_wow64_ntdll( USHORT machine )
  */
 static ULONG_PTR get_image_address(void)
 {
-#ifdef HAVE_GETAUXVAL
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* ⚠ A title has no auxiliary vector, and this console's getauxval does
+     * not answer that with 0 -- it faults:
+     *
+     *     fault signal=0xb addr=0x0 rip=0x8008ef49a  (__getauxval)
+     *
+     * Report no image address, which is what every platform without an auxv
+     * does here. Only this caller is affected: the auxv is read in three other
+     * places and all of them are out of reach -- one behind __linux__, two on
+     * the ARM feature paths. */
+    return 0;
+#elif defined(HAVE_GETAUXVAL)
     ULONG_PTR size, num, phdr_addr = getauxval( AT_PHDR );
     ElfW(Phdr) *phdr;
 
-- 
